  summary: { writes: writes.length, done: writes.length - failed, failed } } }];

// Build the write-back to the intake sheet (#355). Only the automation's columns of the rows this run
// decided are written (the roles in Run Settings SHEET_LAYOUT; an optional role set to '' is skipped),
// as RAW values: nothing is ever run as a formula. Layout v2 write rules: DONE and ADOPTED write the
// code, status, end date (a real date: a Sheets date number), made time, customer ID and an empty
// message; every other status writes only status, message and, when one customer matched, the
// customer ID, so the consultant's own code, end-date and created values stay until a code is made. Guard: the sheet is read again just before the write; the columns are found
// again by header, and a row whose invoice, traveller no. or email moved (a row inserted, deleted or
// edited during the run) is not written; the next run puts it right (a code made this run is then found
// and adopted, not made twice). A header change during the run writes nothing.
// ---- the sheet layout: the only place columns come from is Run Settings SHEET_LAYOUT ---- //
// Roles map to header names (row 1). Columns are found by header at run time, so this node holds no
// column name or letter. A required role must name a header that appears exactly once in row 1; an
// optional role may be '' or null (not read or written).
// Without a traveller role there is one code per booking-no. row, named XT-INV<digits> (layout v2, F1 (a));
// with one, codes are XT-INV<digits>-<NN> and traveller 1 also matches the old name XT-INV<digits>.
